# Student Dashboard Page & Dropdown Filters

The main student dashboard UI is implemented in [medshadow/src/app/dashboard/student/page.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/app/dashboard/student/page.tsx). It features:

- A fixed header with navigation and a user avatar dropdown menu (profile/sign out)
- A sticky search/filter bar directly below the header, with `overflow-visible` and `rounded-lg` to prevent dropdown clipping
- Filter controls for Type, Specialty, Location, and Duration, each using the [DropdownFilter](mdc:medshadow/src/components/DropdownFilter.tsx) component
- The sidebar and main content area are flex containers, with the sidebar containing stats, sorting, and a scrollable opportunity list

## DropdownFilter Component
- All dropdowns use [DropdownFilter.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/DropdownFilter.tsx)
- Dropdowns are accessible, close on outside click, and use a checkmark icon for selection
- The 'Clear' button is at the top right of the dropdown
- For 'Specialty' and 'Location', the dropdown is wider (`w-72`), uses a larger font, and includes a search bar to filter options in real time
- Selected options are highlighted with a background and bold text

## CSS/UX Notes
- The sticky search bar uses `overflow-visible` to ensure dropdowns are never clipped
- No parent container uses `overflow-hidden` or similar, so dropdowns are always fully visible
- The UI is responsive and mobile-friendly

Refer to these files for any changes to dashboard layout, dropdown UX, or filter logic.

## Required APIs
- User profile fetch: `GET /api/user/profile` (for user info/avatar)
- Applications list: `GET /api/applications` (for sidebar stats)
- Saved opportunities: `GET /api/opportunities/saved` (for sidebar stats)
- Opportunities list: `GET /api/opportunities` (for main/filterable list)
- (Future) Opportunity apply: `POST /api/applications` (for Apply button)
- (Future) Opportunity save/unsave: `POST /api/opportunities/saved` (for Save button)
- (Future) Opportunity filters: `GET /api/opportunities?type=...&specialty=...` (for search/filter)
- (Future) User sign out: (NextAuth or custom endpoint)

See [API endpoints guide](mdc:reference/api-endpoints.js) and [database schema](mdc:reference/database-schema.js) for details.

