# Student Dashboard Implementation

## Overview
The student dashboard is implemented in [medshadow/src/app/dashboard/student/page.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/app/dashboard/student/page.tsx) using a modular component architecture. The page is built using Next.js with TypeScript and follows the app router pattern.

## Component Structure
The dashboard is composed of several reusable components located in `medshadow/src/components/dashboard/`:

- [MainContent.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/MainContent.tsx): Main content area that displays either an empty state or opportunity details
- [OpportunityDetails.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/OpportunityDetails.tsx): Detailed view of a selected opportunity
- [Sidebar.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/Sidebar.tsx): Left sidebar containing filters and opportunity list
- [OpportunityList.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/OpportunityList.tsx): List of opportunity cards
- [OpportunityListItem.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/OpportunityListItem.tsx): Individual opportunity card component
- [StatsQuickActions.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/StatsQuickActions.tsx): Quick stats and action buttons
- [SortDropdown.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/components/dashboard/SortDropdown.tsx): Dropdown for sorting opportunities

## Key Features

### Authentication & Authorization
- JWT-based authentication
- Role-based access (student-only)
- Automatic redirect to signin for unauthenticated users

### Opportunity Management
- List view with filtering and sorting
- Detailed opportunity view
- Save/Apply functionality
- Distance-based filtering using Haversine formula

### UI/UX Features
- Responsive design (mobile-first)
- Collapsible sidebar on mobile
- Loading states
- Empty states
- Modern styling using Tailwind CSS

### Data Flow
1. Page loads and checks authentication
2. Fetches user details, applications, and saved opportunities
3. Maintains list of opportunities with filtering/sorting state
4. Updates filtered/sorted list based on user interactions

## Component Props

### Sidebar Props
```typescript
{
  applicationsCount: number;
  savedCount: number;
  sortOption: 'distance' | 'date' | '';
  setSortOption: (option: 'distance' | 'date' | '') => void;
  sortedOpportunities: Opportunity[];
  selectedOpportunity: Opportunity | null;
  setSelectedOpportunity: (opp: Opportunity | null) => void;
  sortDropdownOpen: boolean;
  setSortDropdownOpen: (open: boolean) => void;
}
```

### MainContent Props
```typescript
{
  selectedOpportunity: Opportunity | null;
}
```

## State Management
The dashboard uses React's useState and useEffect hooks for state management:
- User authentication state
- Selected opportunity
- Filter/sort preferences
- UI state (sidebar visibility, dropdowns)

